#X text 30 20 With the 'savestate' message or the '-savestate' flag the GUI operates in 'save state mode' \, where it saves the selected tab from the last time the patch was saved. Note that this is only useful for patches and not abstractions. For abstractions you should use [savestate] instead \, and also have a look at [presets]. Unlike iemguis \, the value is not output when loading the patch \, use [loadbang] for that., f 62;
#X obj 60 175 tgl 19 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 #dcdcdc #000000 #000000 0 1;
#X msg 60 205 savestate \$1;
#X obj 60 245 else/tab 200 24 4 -savestate;
